>>>
>>>
>>> Sorry, on desktop the top bar doesn't look quite like
>>> http://imgur.com/aJqUirM but the layout does look similarly
>>> cramped/broken at very small window sizes.
>>>
>>
>> MobileFrontend tries to detect true mobile devices to disable this
>> Metrolook skin and to enable its own skin. http://imgur.com/aJqUirM is
>> done from a real phone (i.e. not browser console emulation)
>>
>
> The current situation is even worse: http://imgur.com/gGP8Y0D
>
> I suggest that for devices with such narrow screens the right block is put
> to the top (so that language changing block can be seen) with news hidden.
>
> Or if you need news even on mobile devices then the whole right block can
> be split into two blocks moving languages to the top (so that new visitors
> can immediately change to their language) and news to the bottom so they
> dont distract new visitors with lots of guest-unfriendly unfamiliar
> information.
>

Another solution can be just placing the language block back to top as it
was done by me long before LMW became official. It'd take two lines of
text. Not too much IMO (the left sidebar and the top toolbar aren't
scrollable so scrolling the content of the page doesn't make you lose main
wiki controls).
The new block thus would become independent and can be assigned a separate
CSS/JS for narrow devices.


